"""Select every requested manuscript row and record the exact disposition."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,re,json
base=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
source=base/'background/companion/DER_I-b/DER_I-b_claims.csv'
rows=list(csv.DictReader(source.open()))
selected=[r for r in rows if r['proof_status'] in ('false','conjectured') and 76<=int(re.search(r'\d+',r['ms_page']).group())<=126]
D={
'I-b-A069':('Proved for HOT and all-derivator strengthened gluing','D.10; D.11; B.3; B.5','The specified fork preserves the HOT condition. For every Der1-4 derivator, Wlc is a fundamental localizer; its cosieve-gluing step follows in the accessible sublocalizer generated by the inclusion.','The all-derivator W1 gluing step follows from B.5 Loc6a. This concerns the specified fork, not all base changes of the original weak condition.'),
'I-b-B079-03':('Refuted; precise weaker repair Proved','D.2; D.4; D.12','Input Wlc to a universal weak fibration yields a WD output, not automatically Wlc. A HOT C2-gerbe pulls back a Wlc point-to-S2 equivalence to a non-Wlc fibre inclusion.','Input W1 yields WD. If all local-system direct images are controlled and Wcoh=W1 (enhanced case), both input and output can be W1.'),
'I-b-B079-04':('Refuted; dual weaker repair Proved','D.2; D.4; D.12','Same Wlc failure and dual left-Kan repair; universal hypotheses include all base changes.','Dual of the preceding W1 repair, using homological comparisons.'),
'I-b-B079-07':('Refuted','D.12; D.4','False for sets before replacement by the regular cover EG→BG; still false for Wlc-only restricted fibration repair by the finite gerbe.','After replacing the comma tests by W1 and using the enhanced equality with cohomological equivalences, universal W1 preservation holds; this is a stronger definition.'),
'I-b-B081-04':('Refuted for weak and 2-complete variants','D.3; D.4; D.2','The rational weak composition example and the finite set-valued 2-complete composition example are verified.','The complete cohomological class composes. In the enhanced setting it is the W1 version; universal W1 preservation is formally composable.'),
'I-b-B084-01':('Proved','D.7','Every universal WD equivalence is fully faithful on the whole D(B); universal Wlc is sufficient by inclusion.','Universal W1 is also sufficient by inclusion. All small comma/factorization/disjoint-union shapes are required.'),
'I-b-B084-06':('Refuted for blanket substitutions; model-fibration repair Known','D.5; D.6','Finite C2-gerbe H→K has Wlc-equivalent totals over a completely set-aspherical base, but fibre BC2→e is not Wlc. Accessible Wlc Thomason model fibrations restore the assertion.','Even universal W1-preserving fibrations need not have total-to-fibre detection: reversed transport BC2→e with its section. For HOT structural fibrations, W1 detection does hold under enhancement.'),
'I-b-B084-07':('Refuted for blanket substitutions','D.5','The gerbe base K has the homotopy type of S2 and is completely Set-aspherical, so complete base asphericity alone does not repair the Wlc assertion.','The reversed-transport example has base [1], already contractible; complete base asphericity does not repair this W1 fibration interpretation either.'),
'I-b-B087-05':('Refuted','D.9','Automorphisms of a trivial two-sheet bundle remain; replace unique isomorphism by an isomorphism class with the chosen framing/conjugacy convention.','Independent of coefficient class.'),
'I-b-B093-04':('Refuted','D.9','E=G discrete regular and reflected circle Z satisfy the stated hypotheses but total quotient is Z and the fibre inclusion is the identity, hence in Wlc.','Identity counterexample also rules out asserted failure of W1.'),
'I-b-B093-05':('Refuted','D.9','The E=G example works even with completely aspherical base. The manuscript S2/S1 specialization has residual rational H3, verified in a finite categorical model.','Failure of WD already precludes W1 and Wlc; changing their names cannot remove the missing tensor cross term.'),
'I-b-B095-01':('Refuted','D.9','Correct orbit relations are p1- p0- = p1+ p0+ and p1- p0+ = p1+ p0-.','Composition-law error independent of localizer; all four sign products checked.'),
'I-b-B096-04':('Proved under stated axiom','D.8; D.2','Der3 a-prime makes local systems constant on weakly contractible test bases; exact fibre/base-change argument proves the weak-condition equivalence. B.3 supplies relative categorical descent, while the composition counterexamples still prohibit the blanket Wlc substitution.','Enhanced W1 identifies with cohomological equivalence and uses the all-local-coefficients version.'),
'Ib-C003':('Refuted','D.9','The proper cosieve {1}→[1] has empty and terminal comma categories; the transition is not Wlc.','The transition is not W1 either. Properness must be supplemented by a transport condition.'),
'Ib-C021':('Known','D.8','For HOT all classes equal W-infinity; replacing equivalence by Wlc leaves the statement true.','Same for W1; mapping-space Yoneda and Cisinski Corollary3.8.'),
'Ib-C026':('Known','D.8','Cisinski Corollary3.8 proves local-system equivalence for every derivator under a nerve weak equivalence.','Full faithfulness and both local (co)homology comparisons follow by adjunction.'),
'Ib-C048':('Known','D.8','All five HOT equivalence notions equal W-infinity.','Same.'),
'Ib-C069':('Known','D.8','HOT restricted, universal weak, and universal W-infinity-preserving fibration notions coincide.','No difference because all HOT equivalence classes agree.'),
'Ib-C082':('Refuted','D.9','Internal Homs do not make a constant equivalence full. e→BC2 over Q and trivial/sign representations give the failure. A Wlc hypothesis implies fullness tautologically.','Restore adjective cohomological; compatible locally constant internal Homs then prove full faithfulness. Use the monoidal unit, not a stable terminal zero.'),
'Ib-C092':('Known','D.8','HOT satisfies c-double-prime: W_HOT=W-infinity=W_HOT-lc.','Same.'),
'Ib-C096':('Known with precise notion','D.8; D.6','Chapter XI intrinsic HOT-fibrations are universal W-infinity-preserving sharp maps. They need not be the Thomason model fibrations.','The unique reasonable language is interpreted as the specific equivalences of definitions, not uniqueness among every possible fibration class.')
}
assert set(D)=={r['id'] for r in selected},(set(D)^{r['id'] for r in selected})
fields=['manuscript_id','ms_page','original_status','original_statement','disposition','where_proved','two_complete_version','one_complete_version']
out=base/'GALOIS/research/D_audit.csv'
with out.open('w',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader()
 for r in selected:
  status,where,two,one=D[r['id']]
  w.writerow(dict(manuscript_id=r['id'],ms_page=r['ms_page'],original_status=r['proof_status'],original_statement=r['statement'],disposition=status,where_proved=where,two_complete_version=two,one_complete_version=one))
print(json.dumps({'source_rows':len(rows),'selected_false_or_conjectured_rows_76_to_126':len(selected),'dispositions':len(D),'missing_rows':[],'output':str(out.relative_to(base))},indent=2))
